> Using SNAPS-OS Functions

## TLDR TUI

call using *SUPER+H* or the alias `tldrtui`

use mouse or arrow keys. type to search.

pressing enter or double-clicking an entry opens the man page.

pressing q on the manpage returns to the main menu.

to exit, press *SUPER+Q* to close the terminal.

## Help TUI

call using *SUPER+SHIFT+H* or the alias `helptui`

use arrow keys or mouse to navigate, type to search.

enter refreshes the menu.

to exit, press *SUPER+Q*.

## Mango Config Editor

press *SUPER+M* or run `mangoconf`

shows a menu listing config files in ~/.config/mango with a preview on the right.

press enter on a file to open it in micro.

in micro, use ctrl+s to save and ctrl+q to quit.

then reload mango config with *SUPER+R*.

## Project Selector

uses a state file at ~/.config/projectdir.state to determine which directory to scan.

default directory is ~/projects. to change:
`echo "my-projects/subdir" > ~/.config/projectdir.state`

only displays git repositories.

open with *SUPER+SHIFT+TAB* or the alias `git-projects`

left side shows full repo paths, right side shows file listing and readme.

pressing enter opens the repo in code-oss.

## Layout Switcher

open with *SUPER+SHIFT+W*

arrow keys to browse, enter to select.

affects only your current view on the active monitor.

reset to dwindle by pressing *SUPER+R*.

## Documentation Menu

open with the alias `documentation` or *SUPER+SHIFT+M*

provides quick access to documentation sites in firefox and searchable quick reference menus.

## Wallpaper Switcher

open with *SUPER+W*, shows directories in ~/.config/snapsos/wallpapers

each directory can contain any number of images (cycled through). one image = no cycling.

cycle forward/back with *alt+W* and *shift+alt+W*.

## Bar Presets

open with *SUPER+SHIFT+D*, allows toggling pre-included bars and dock, including combination presets.

## Tips

shown automatically on first terminal session, also via `tipme` command.

press *SUPER+0* to get a tip in notifications.

## Package TUIs

Pacman GUI: `pacgui` (alias, no default keybind)
AUR GUI: `aurgui` (alias, no default keybind)

Both use FZF with multi-select via tab. Search, tab to select, enter to install.

Always prefer pacman repositories first, then AUR, then flatpak.
